			"notes": "## Argentum\n\n### New\n\n- rewrite the text renderer, with support for modern font json providers (bitmap, space, reference and unihex). the old ascii sheet stays as a fallback\n- direct rendering: frames draw straight to the window instead of through minecraft's framebuffer whenever nothing needs it\n- fast particles\n- new quad-relative vertex format\n- rgss texture filtering\n- sky fog: distant terrain fades into the sky behind it instead of a flat fog color\n- experimental borderless fullscreen on windows\n- raise the fps limit to 1500\n- mipmap level changes now apply without a restart\n\n### Performance Improvements\n\n- fast name tags (previously name tag batching): name tag text is cached and instanced\n- faster particle culling\n- even faster clouds\n- entity lighting moved into the instancing shader, which fixes a big fps drop when the camera is inside an entity\n- armor glint reuses the armor piece it was already given instead of rendering the model again\n- hurt entities no longer reprogram the texture combiners for every model pass when instanced (much faster in fights)\n- entity occlusion queries are shared between nearby entities and adapt to camera speed\n- sign text bakes in more cases: hd and mcpatcher fonts, smoothed fonts, right-to-left languages, underlined and struck-through text\n- fully transparent hud fills are skipped\n- terrain, entity and weather shaders are kept across world changes\n\n### Fixes\n\n- entities faded by other mods rendered opaque\n- the edges of the sky were visible above 24 chunks render distance\n- the lower sky looked wrong during sunsets\n- z-fighting on some emissive entity layers\n- armor and item glint on mesa drivers\n- entity shadows behaving differently from vanilla with batching on\n\n## Argentum Extras\n\n- add toggles for beacon beams, enchanting table books, moving pistons, item frames and paintings\n- add a force sky option, which renders the sky and sunrise below 4 chunks render distance\n- add an option to hide achievement toasts\n- the sky is skipped entirely when every sky element is turned off\n- sky toggles now also apply to cera's custom skies\n- the lower sky is on by default\n- fix block outline width settings not resetting properly\n\n## Cera\n\n### new\n\n- shader pack support for optifine-format packs, compatiblity with optifine 1.8.9\n- custom entity models, including animations, random models, per-type skull models, held items attached to custom parts and modern entity names\n- optifine cosmetics are now built with the CEM part parser\n- emissive entity layers\n\n### fixed\n\n- respect night vision strength\n- fall back to optifine's default sky axis when a custom sky doesn't set one\n- a crash when rendering dropped air items"
		},
